#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:2
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configure &kappname;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:3
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Selecting <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure "
"<replaceable>Application</replaceable>...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from "
"the menu brings up the <guilabel>Configure</guilabel> dialog box. This "
"dialog can be used to alter a number of different settings. The settings "
"available for change vary according to which category the user chooses from "
"a vertical list on the left side of the dialog. By means of three buttons "
"along the bottom of the box the user can control the process."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:13
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You may invoke the <guilabel>Help</guilabel> system, accept the current "
"settings and close the dialog by means of the <guibutton>OK</guibutton> "
"button, or <guibutton>Cancel</guibutton> the process. The categories "
"<guilabel>Appearance</guilabel>, <guilabel>Fonts &amp; Colors</guilabel>, "
"<guilabel>Editing</guilabel>, <guilabel>Open/Save</guilabel> and "
"<guilabel>Extensions</guilabel> are detailed below."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:24
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Editor Component Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:25
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This group contains all pages related to the editor component of &kappname;. "
"Most of the settings here are defaults, they can be overridden by <link "
"linkend=\"pref-open-save-modes-filetypes\">defining a filetype</link>, by "
"<link linkend=\"config-variables\">Document Variables</link> or by changing "
"them per document during an editing session."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:31
#, no-c-format
msgid "Appearance"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:34 configuring.docbook:534 configuring.docbook:922
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>General</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:38
#, no-c-format
msgid "Dynamic Word Wrap"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:40
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is checked, the text lines will be wrapped at the view border "
"on the screen."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:44
#, no-c-format
msgid "Dynamic word wrap indicators (if applicable)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:45
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Choose when the Dynamic word wrap indicators should be displayed, either "
"<guilabel>Off</guilabel>, <guilabel>Follow Line Numbers</guilabel> or "
"<guilabel>Always on</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:50
#, no-c-format
msgid "Align dynamically wrapped lines to indentation depth:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:53
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Enables the start of dynamically wrapped lines to be aligned vertically to "
"the indentation level of the first line. This can help to make code and "
"markup more readable."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:56
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Additionally, this allows you to set a maximum width of the screen, as a "
"percentage, after which dynamically wrapped lines will no longer be "
"vertically aligned. For example, at 50%, lines whose indentation levels are "
"deeper than 50% of the width of the screen will not have vertical alignment "
"applied to subsequent wrapped lines."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:68
#, no-c-format
msgid "Whitespace Highlighting"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:72
#, no-c-format
msgid "Highlight tabulators"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:73
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The editor will display a &raquo; symbol to indicate the presence of a tab "
"in the text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:77
#, no-c-format
msgid "Highlight trailing spaces"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:78
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The editor will display dots to indicate the presence of extra whitespace at "
"the end of lines."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:86
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Advanced</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:91
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show indentation lines"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:93
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this is checked, the editor will display vertical lines to help "
"identifying indent lines."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:97
#, no-c-format
msgid "Highlight range between selected brackets"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:99
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this is enabled, the range between the selected matching brackets will be "
"highlighted."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:105
#, no-c-format
msgid "Animate bracket matching"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:107
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If enabled, moving on the brackets (<keycap>{</keycap>, <keycap>[</keycap>, "
"<keycap>]</keycap>, <keycap>}</keycap>,<keycap>(</keycap> or <keycap>)</"
"keycap>) will quickly animate the matching bracket."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:112
#, no-c-format
msgid "Fold first line"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:114
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If enabled, the first line is folded, if possible. This is useful, if the "
"file starts with a comment, such as a copyright"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:121
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Borders</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:125
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Borders</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show folding markers"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:131
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is checked, the current view will display marks for code "
"folding, if code folding is available."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:135
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show icon border"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:137
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this is checked, you will see an icon border on the left hand side. The "
"icon border shows bookmark signs for instance."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:141
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show line numbers"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:143
#, no-c-format
msgid "If this is checked, you will see line numbers on the left hand side."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:147
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show line modification markers"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:149
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this is checked, line modification markers will be visible. For more "
"information, see <xref linkend=\"kate-part-line-modification\"/>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:154
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show scrollbar marks"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:156
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is checked the current view will show marks on the vertical "
"scrollbar. These marks will for instance show bookmarks."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:161
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show scrollbar mini-map"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:162
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is checked, every new view will show a mini map of the "
"document on the vertical scrollbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:164
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For more information on the scrollbar minimap, see <xref linkend=\"kate-part-"
"scrollbar-minimap\"/>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:168
#, no-c-format
msgid "Minimap Width"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:169
#, no-c-format
msgid "Adjusts the width of the scrollbar mini-map, defined in pixels."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:177
#, no-c-format
msgid "Sort Bookmarks Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:182
#, no-c-format
msgid "By creation"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:184
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Each new bookmark will be added to the bottom, independently from where it "
"is placed in the document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:188
#, no-c-format
msgid "By position"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:190
#, no-c-format
msgid "The bookmarks will be ordered by the line numbers they are placed at."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:202
#, no-c-format
msgid "Fonts &amp; Colors"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:204
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This section of the dialog lets you configure all fonts and colors in any "
"color scheme you have, as well creating new schemes or deleting existing "
"ones. Each scheme has settings for colors, fonts and normal and highlight "
"text styles."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:210
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kappname; will preselect the currently active scheme for you, if you want "
"to work on a different scheme start by selecting that from the "
"<guilabel>Schema</guilabel> combobox. With the <guibutton>New</guibutton> "
"and <guibutton>Delete</guibutton> button you can create a new scheme or "
"delete existing ones."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:214
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"At the bottom of the page you can select the <guilabel>Default schema for "
"&kappname;</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:216
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By default, &kappname; will base its color scheme on the current &kde; color "
"scheme. You can reset an individual color back to default by clicking the "
"reset arrow to the right of the entry in the color editor, or you can reset "
"all colors back to default by clicking the <guibutton>Use &kde; Color "
"Scheme</guibutton> at the bottom of the panel."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:223
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can adjust the &kde; color scheme in the <ulink url=\"help:/kcontrol/"
"colors/\"><guilabel>Colors</guilabel> module in &systemsettings;</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:229
#, no-c-format
msgid "Colors"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:233
#, no-c-format
msgid "Editor Background Colors"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:239
#, no-c-format
msgid "Text Area"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:240
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is the default background for the editor area, it will be the dominant "
"color on the editor area."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:245
#, no-c-format
msgid "Selected Text"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:246
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is the background for selected text. The default is the global "
"selection color, as set in your &kde; color preferences."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:252
#, no-c-format
msgid "Current Line"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:253
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Set the color for the current line. Setting this a bit different from the "
"Normal text background helps to keep focus on the current line."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:259
#, no-c-format
msgid "Search Highlight"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:260
#, no-c-format
msgid "Set the color for the text that matches your last search."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:265
#, no-c-format
msgid "Replace Highlight"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:266
#, no-c-format
msgid "Set the color for the text that matches your last replace operation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:275
#, no-c-format
msgid "Icon Border"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:280
#, no-c-format
msgid "Background Area"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:281
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This color is used for the marks, line numbers and folding marker borders in "
"the left side of the editor view when they are displayed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:287
#, no-c-format
msgid "Line Numbers"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:288
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This color is used to draw the line numbers on the left side of the view "
"when displayed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:295
#, no-c-format
msgid "Word Wrap Marker"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:296
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This color is used to draw a pattern to the left of dynamically wrapped "
"lines when those are aligned vertically, as well as for the static word wrap "
"marker."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:302
#, no-c-format
msgid "Code Folding"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:303
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This color is used to highlight the section of code that would be folded "
"when you click on the code folding arrow to the left of a document. For more "
"information, see <link linkend=\"advanced-editing-tools-code-folding\">the "
"code folding documentation</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:311
#, no-c-format
msgid "Modified Lines"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:312
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This color is used to highlight to the left of a document lines that have "
"been modified but not yet saved. For more information, see <xref linkend="
"\"kate-part-line-modification\"/>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:318
#, no-c-format
msgid "Saved Lines"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:319
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This color is used to highlight to the left of a document lines that have "
"been modified this session and saved. For more information, see <xref "
"linkend=\"kate-part-line-modification\"/>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:329
#, no-c-format
msgid "Text Decorations"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:334
#, no-c-format
msgid "Spelling Mistake Line"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:335
#, no-c-format
msgid "This color is used to indicate spelling mistakes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:339
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tab and Space Markers"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:340
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This color is used to draw white space indicators, when they are enabled."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:345
#, no-c-format
msgid "Indentation Line"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:346
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This color is used to draw a line to the left of indented blocks, if <link "
"linkend=\"appearance-general\">that feature is enabled</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:351
#, no-c-format
msgid "Bracket Highlight"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:352
#, no-c-format
msgid "This color is used to draw the background of matching brackets."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:361
#, no-c-format
msgid "Marker Colors"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:366
#, no-c-format
msgid "Bookmark"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:367
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This color is used to indicate bookmarks. For more information, see <xref "
"linkend=\"kate-part-bookmarks\"/>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:372
#, no-c-format
msgid "Active Breakpoint"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:373
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This color is used by the GDB plugin to indicate an active breakpoint. For "
"more information, see <ulink url=\"help:/kate/kate-application-plugin-gdb."
"html\">the GDB Plugin documentation</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:380
#, no-c-format
msgid "Reached Breakpoint"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:381
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This color is used by the GDB plugin to indicate a breakpoint you have "
"reached while debugging. For more information, see <ulink url=\"help:/kate/"
"kate-application-plugin-gdb.html\">the GDB Plugin documentation</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:388
#, no-c-format
msgid "Disabled Breakpoint"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:389
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This color is used by the GDB plugin to indicate an inactive breakpoint. For "
"more information, see <ulink url=\"help:/kate/kate-application-plugin-gdb."
"html\">the GDB Plugin documentation</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:396
#, no-c-format
msgid "Execution"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:397
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This color is used by the GDB plugin the line presently being executed. For "
"more information, see <ulink url=\"help:/kate/kate-application-plugin-gdb."
"html\">the GDB Plugin documentation</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:404
#, no-c-format
msgid "Warning"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:405
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This color is used by the build plugin to indicate a line that has caused a "
"compiler warning. For more information, see <ulink url=\"help:/kate/kate-"
"application-plugin-build.html\">the Build Plugin documentation</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:412
#, no-c-format
msgid "Error"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:413
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This color is used by the build plugin to indicate a line that has caused a "
"compiler error. For more information, see <ulink url=\"help:/kate/kate-"
"application-plugin-build.html\">the Build Plugin documentation</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:424
#, no-c-format
msgid "Text Templates &amp; Snippets"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:429
#, no-c-format
msgid "Background"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:430
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This color is used by the &kate; Snippets plugin to mark the background of a "
"snippet."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:437
#, no-c-format
msgid "Editable Placeholder"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:438
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This color is used by the &kate; Snippets plugin to mark a placeholder that "
"you can click in to edit manually."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:445
#, no-c-format
msgid "Focused Editable Placeholder"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:446
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This color is used by the &kate; Snippets plugin to mark the placeholder "
"that you are presently editing."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:453
#, no-c-format
msgid "Not Editable Placeholder"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:454
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This color is used by the &kate; Snippets plugin to mark a placeholder that "
"cannot be edited manually, such as one that is automatically populated. For "
"more information, see <ulink url=\"help:/kate/kate-application-plugin-"
"snippets.html\">the &kate; Snippets documentation</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: configuring.docbook:466
#, no-c-format
msgid "Use &kde; Color Scheme"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:468
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Clicking this button will set all the above defined colors to match the "
"current color scheme defined in &kde;'s &systemsettings;. For more "
"information, see <ulink url=\"help:/kcontrol/colors/\">the documentation for "
"the Colors &kde; Control Module</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:472
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you do not use the &kde; &plasma; Workspaces, this button will have no "
"effect, and may not be present."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:481
#, no-c-format
msgid "Font"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:482
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you can choose the font for the schema. You can choose from any font "
"available on your system, and set a default size. A sample text displays at "
"the bottom of the dialog, so you can see the effect of your choices."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:487
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For more information about selecting a font, see the <ulink url=\"help:/"
"fundamentals/fonts.html\"><emphasis>Choosing Fonts</emphasis> section of the "
"<emphasis>&kde; Fundamentals</emphasis> documentation</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:493
#, no-c-format
msgid "Default Text Styles"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:494
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The default text styles are inherited by the highlight text styles, allowing "
"the editor to present text in a very consistent way, for example comment "
"text is using the same style in almost all of the text formats that "
"&kappname; can highlight."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:498 configuring.docbook:513
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The name in the list of styles is using the style configured for the item, "
"providing you with an immediate preview when configuring a style."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:501
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Each style lets you select common attributes as well as foreground and "
"background colors. To unset a background color, right-click to use the "
"context menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:507
#, no-c-format
msgid "Highlighting Text Styles"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:508
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you can edit the text styles used by a specific highlight definition. "
"The editor preselects the highlight used by your current document. To work "
"on a different highlight, select one in the <guilabel>Highlight</guilabel> "
"combobox above the style list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:516
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Each style lets you select common attributes as well as foreground and "
"background colors. To unset a background color, right-click to use the "
"context menu. In addition you can see if a style is equal to the default "
"style used for the item, and set it to that if not."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:520
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You will notice that many highlights contain other highlights represented by "
"groups in the style list. For example most highlights import the Alert "
"highlight, and many source code formats imports the Doxygen highlight. "
"Editing colors in those groups only affects the styles when used in the "
"edited highlight format."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:531
#, no-c-format
msgid "Editing"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:538
#, no-c-format
msgid "Static Word Wrap"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:539
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Word wrap is a feature that causes the editor to automatically start a new "
"line of text and move (wrap) the cursor to the beginning of that new line. "
"&kappname; will automatically start a new line of text when the current line "
"reaches the length specified by the <link linkend=\"pref-wrap-words-at"
"\">Wrap Words At:</link> option."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:547
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enable static word wrap"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:549
#, no-c-format
msgid "Turns static word wrap on or off."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:553
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show static word wrap marker (if applicable)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:556
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is checked, a vertical line will be drawn at the word wrap "
"column as defined in the <menuchoice> <guimenu>Settings</guimenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Configure Editor...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> in the Editing "
"tab. Please note that the word wrap marker is only drawn if you use a fixed "
"pitch font."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:564
#, no-c-format
msgid "Wrap words at:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:566
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the <link linkend=\"pref-word-wrap\">Enable static word wrap</link> "
"option is selected this entry determines the length (in characters) at which "
"the editor will automatically start a new line."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:575
#, no-c-format
msgid "Input Mode"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:575
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The selected input mode will be enabled when opening a new view. You can "
"still toggle the vi input mode on/off for a particular view in the "
"<guimenu>Edit</guimenu> menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:583
#, no-c-format
msgid "Auto brackets"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:583
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When the user types a left bracket (<keycap>[</keycap>, <keycap>(</keycap>, "
"or <keycap>{</keycap>) &kappname; automatically enters the right bracket "
"(<keycap>}</keycap>, <keycap>)</keycap>, or <keycap>]</keycap>) to the right "
"of the cursor."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:587
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When text is selected, typing one of the characters wraps the selected text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:593
#, no-c-format
msgid "Copy and Paste"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:597
#, no-c-format
msgid "Copy/Cut the current line if no selection"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:598
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is enabled and the text selection is empty, copy and cut "
"action are performed for the line of text at the actual cursor position."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:609
#, no-c-format
msgid "Text Navigation"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:614
#, no-c-format
msgid "Text Cursor Movement"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:618
#, no-c-format
msgid "Smart home and smart end"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:620
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When selected, pressing the home key will cause the cursor to skip white "
"space and go to the start of a line's text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:625
#, no-c-format
msgid "PageUp/PageDown moves cursor"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:627
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This option changes the behavior of the cursor when the user presses the "
"<keycap>Page Up</keycap> or <keycap>Page Down</keycap> key. If unselected "
"the text cursor will maintain its relative position within the visible text "
"in &kappname; as new text becomes visible as a result of the operation. So "
"if the cursor is in the middle of the visible text when the operation occurs "
"it will remain there (except when one reaches the beginning or end.) With "
"this option selected, the first key press will cause the cursor to move to "
"either the top or bottom of the visible text as a new page of text is "
"displayed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:638
#, no-c-format
msgid "Autocenter cursor:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:640
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Sets the number of lines to maintain visible above and below the cursor when "
"possible."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:649
#, no-c-format
msgid "Text Selection Mode"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:653
#, no-c-format
msgid "Normal"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:655
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Selections will be overwritten by typed text and will be lost on cursor "
"movement."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:660
#, no-c-format
msgid "Persistent"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:662
#, no-c-format
msgid "Selections will stay even after cursor movement and typing."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:666
#, no-c-format
msgid "Allow scrolling past the end of the document"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:667
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This option lets you scroll past the end of the document. This can be used "
"to vertically centre the bottom of the document, or put it on top of the "
"current view."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:678
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "Introduction"
msgid "Indentation"
msgstr "Inföhren"

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:683
#, no-c-format
msgid "Default indentation mode:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:685
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select the automatic indentation mode you want to use as default. It is "
"strongly recommended to use <userinput>None</userinput> or "
"<userinput>Normal</userinput> here, and use filetype configurations to set "
"other indentation modes for text formats like C/C++ code or &XML;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:693
#, no-c-format
msgid "Indent using"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:697
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tabulators"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:699
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When this is enabled the editor will insert tabulator characters when you "
"press the &Tab; key or use <link linkend=\"kate-part-autoindent\">automatic "
"indentation</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:705
#, no-c-format
msgid "Spaces"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:707
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When this is enabled the editor will insert a calculated number of spaces "
"according to the position in the text and the <option>tab-width</option> "
"setting when you press the &Tab; key or use <link linkend=\"kate-part-"
"autoindent\">automatic indentation</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:714
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tabulators and Spaces"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:716
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When this is enabled, the editor will insert spaces as describe above when "
"indenting or pressing &Tab; at the beginning of a line, but insert "
"tabulators when the &Tab; key is pressed in the middle or end of a line."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:722
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tab width:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:724
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This configures the number of spaces that are displayed in place of a "
"tabulator character."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:729
#, no-c-format
msgid "Indentation width:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:731
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The indentation width is the number of spaces which is used to indent a "
"line. If configured to indent using tabulators, a tabulator character is "
"inserted if the indentation is divisible by the tab width."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:741
#, no-c-format
msgid "Indentation Properties"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:745
#, no-c-format
msgid "Keep extra spaces"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:746
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is disabled, changing the indentation level aligns a line to "
"a multiple of the width specified in <guilabel>Indentation width</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:751
#, no-c-format
msgid "Adjust indentation of text pasted from the clipboard"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:753
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is selected, text pasted from the clipboard is indented. "
"Triggering the <guimenuitem>Undo</guimenuitem> action removes the "
"indentation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:762
#, no-c-format
msgid "Indentation Actions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:766
#, no-c-format
msgid "Backspace key in leading blank space unindents"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:768
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is selected, the &Backspace; key decreases the indentation "
"level if the cursor is located in the leading blank space of a line."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:773
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tab key action (if no selection exists)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:775
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want &Tab; to align the current line in the current code block like "
"in emacs, make &Tab; a shortcut to the action <guimenuitem>Align</"
"guimenuitem>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:781
#, no-c-format
msgid "Always advance to the next tab position"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:783
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is selected, the &Tab; key always inserts white space so that "
"the next tab position is reached. If the option <guilabel>Insert spaces "
"instead of tabulators</guilabel> on the <guilabel>General</guilabel> tab in "
"the <guilabel>Editing</guilabel> page is enabled, spaces are inserted; "
"otherwise, a single tabulator is inserted."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:790
#, no-c-format
msgid "Always increase indentation level"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:792
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is selected, the &Tab; key always indents the current line by "
"the number of character positions specified in <guilabel>Indentation width</"
"guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:798
#, no-c-format
msgid "Increase indentation level if in leading blank space"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:800
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is selected, the &Tab; key either indents the current line or "
"advances to the next tab position. If the insertion point is at or before "
"the first non-space character in the line, or if there is a selection, the "
"current line is indented by the number of character positions specified in "
"<guilabel>Indentation width</guilabel>. If the insertion point is located "
"after the first non-space character in the line and there is no selection, "
"white space is inserted so that the next tab position is reached: if the "
"option <guilabel>Insert spaces instead of tabulators</guilabel> on the "
"<guilabel>General</guilabel> tab in the <guilabel>Editing</guilabel> page is "
"enabled, spaces are inserted; otherwise, a single tabulator is inserted."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:824
#, no-c-format
msgid "Auto Completion"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:827 configuring.docbook:877
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>General</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:831
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enable auto completion"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:833
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If enabled, a word completion box automatically pops up during typing "
"showing a list of text entries to complete the current text under the cursor."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:843
#, no-c-format
msgid "Minimal word length to complete"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:844
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"While typing text, the word completion searches for words in the document "
"starting with the already typed text. This option configures the minimal "
"amount of characters that are needed to make the word completion active and "
"pop up a completion box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:851
#, no-c-format
msgid "Remove tail on complete"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:852
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Remove the tail of a previous word when the completion item is chosen from a "
"list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:857
#, no-c-format
msgid "Keyword completion"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:859
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If enabled, the built-in autocompletion uses the keywords defined by the "
"syntax highlighting."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:868
#, no-c-format
msgid "Spellcheck"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:869
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"These configuration options are described in the documentation for the "
"&systemsettings; module <ulink url=\"help:/kcontrol/spellchecking\">Spell "
"Checker</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:874
#, no-c-format
msgid "Vi Input Mode"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:881
#, no-c-format
msgid "Let Vi commands override Kate shortcuts"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:883
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When selected, Vi commands will override &kappname;'s built-in commands. For "
"example: <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>R</keycap></keycombo> will "
"redo, and override the standard action (showing the search and replace "
"dialog)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:889
#, no-c-format
msgid "Display relative line numbers"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:891
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"if this is enabled, the current line always refers to line 0. Lines above "
"and below increase the line number relatively."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:898
#, no-c-format
msgid "Key Mapping"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:899
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Key mapping is used to change the meaning of typed keys. This allows you to "
"move commands to other keys or make special keypresses for doing a series of "
"commands."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:903
#, no-c-format
msgid "Example:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:904
#, no-c-format
msgid "<keycap>F2</keycap> -> <userinput>I--</userinput> &Esc;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:905
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This will prepend <userinput>I--</userinput> to a line when pressing "
"<keycap>F2</keycap>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:919
#, no-c-format
msgid "Open/Save"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:927
#, no-c-format
msgid "File Format"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:932
#, no-c-format
msgid "Encoding"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:934
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This defines the standard encoding to use to open/save files, if not changed "
"in the open/save dialog or by using a command line option."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:940
#, no-c-format
msgid "Encoding Detection"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:942
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select an item from the drop down box, either to disable autodetection or "
"use <guilabel>Universal</guilabel> to enable autodetection for all "
"encodings. But as this may probably only detect utf-8/utf-16, selecting a "
"region will use custom heuristics for better results. If neither the "
"encoding chosen as standard above, nor the encoding specified in the open/"
"save dialog, nor the encoding specified on command line match the content of "
"the file, this detection will be run."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:953
#, no-c-format
msgid "Fallback Encoding"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:955
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This defines the fallback encoding to try for opening files if neither the "
"encoding chosen as standard above, nor the encoding specified in the open/ "
"save dialog, nor the encoding specified on command line match the content of "
"the file. Before this is used, an attempt will be made to determine the "
"encoding to use by looking for a byte order marker at start of file: if one "
"is found, the right unicode encoding will be chosen; otherwise encoding "
"detection will run, if both fail fallback encoding will be tried."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:966
#, no-c-format
msgid "End of line"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:968
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Choose your preferred end of line mode for your active document. You have "
"the choice between &UNIX;, DOS/&Windows; or Macintosh."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:973
#, no-c-format
msgid "Automatic end of line detection"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:975
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Check this if you want the editor to autodetect the end of line type. The "
"first found end of line type will be used for the whole file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:981
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enable byte order marker"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:983
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The byte order mark is a special sequence at the beginning of unicode "
"encoded documents. It helps editors to open text documents with the correct "
"unicode encoding. For more information see <ulink url=\"http://en.wikipedia."
"org/wiki/Byte_Order_Mark\">Byte Order Mark</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:991
#, no-c-format
msgid "Line Length Limit"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:993
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Unfortunately, due to deficiencies in &Qt;, &kappname; experiences poor "
"performance when working with extremely long lines. For that reason, "
"&kappname; will automatically wrap lines when they are longer than the "
"number of characters specified here. To disable this, set this to "
"<userinput>0</userinput>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:1005
#, no-c-format
msgid "Automatic Cleanups on Save"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:1010
#, no-c-format
msgid "Remove trailing spaces"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:1012
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The editor will automatically eliminate extra spaces at the ends of lines of "
"text while saving the file. You can select <guilabel>Never</guilabel> to "
"disable this functionality, <guilabel>On Modified Lines</guilabel> to do so "
"only on lines that you have modified since you last saved the document, or "
"<guilabel>In Entire Document</guilabel> to remove them unconditionally from "
"the entire document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:1022
#, no-c-format
msgid "Append newline at end of file on save"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:1024
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The editor will automatically append a newline to the end of the file if one "
"is not already present upon saving the file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:1037
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Advanced</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:1041
#, no-c-format
msgid "Backup on Save"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:1042
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Backing up on save will cause &kappname; to copy the disk file to &lt;"
"prefix&gt;&lt;filename&gt;&lt;suffix&gt; before saving changes. The suffix "
"defaults to <emphasis role=\"bold\">~</emphasis> and prefix is empty by "
"default."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:1048
#, no-c-format
msgid "Local files"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:1050
#, no-c-format
msgid "Check this if you want backups of local files when saving."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:1055
#, no-c-format
msgid "Remote files"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:1057
#, no-c-format
msgid "Check this if you want backups of remote files when saving."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:1061
#, no-c-format
msgid "Prefix"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:1063
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enter the prefix to prepend to the backup file names."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:1067
#, no-c-format
msgid "Suffix"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:1069
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enter the suffix to add to the backup file names."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:1073
#, no-c-format
msgid "Swap file options"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:1075
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kappname; is able to recover (most of) what was written after last save in "
"case of a crash or power failure. A swap file (.swp.&lt;filename&gt;) is "
"created after the first editing action on a document. If the user doesn’t "
"save the changes and &kappname; crashes, the swap file remains on the disk. "
"When opening a file, &kappname; checks if there is a swap file for the "
"document and if it is, it asks the user whether he wants to recover the lost "
"data or not. The user has the possibility to view the differences between "
"the original file and the recovered one, too. The swap file is deleted after "
"every save and on normal exit."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:1083
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kappname; syncs the swap files on the disk every 15 seconds, but only if "
"they have changed since the last sync. The user can disable the swap files "
"syncing if he wants, by selecting <guilabel>Disable</guilabel>, but this can "
"lead to more data loss."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:1087
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When enabled, the swap files are saved in the same folder as the file. When "
"<guilabel>Alternative Folder</guilabel> is chosen, swap files are created in "
"the specified folder. This is useful for network file systems to avoid "
"unnecessary network traffic."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:1101
#, no-c-format
msgid "Modes &amp; Filetypes"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:1102
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This page allows you to override the default configuration for documents of "
"specified mimetypes. When the editor loads a document, it will try if it "
"matches the file masks or mimetypes for one of the defined filetypes, and if "
"so apply the variables defined. If more filetypes match, the one with the "
"highest priority will be used."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:1110
#, no-c-format
msgid "Filetype:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:1111 configuring.docbook:1131
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The filetype with the highest priority is the one displayed in the first "
"drop down box. If more filetypes were found, they are also listed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:1116
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>New</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:1117
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is used to create a new filetype. After you click on this button, the "
"fields below get empty and you can fill the properties you want for the new "
"filetype."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:1122
#, no-c-format
msgid "Delete"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:1123
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To remove an existing filetype, select it from the drop down box and press "
"the Delete button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:1130
#, no-c-format
msgid "Properties of <replaceable>current filetype</replaceable>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:1136
#, no-c-format
msgid "Name:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:1137
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The name of the filetype will be the text of the corresponding menu item. "
"This name is displayed in the <menuchoice><guimenu>Tools</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Filetypes</guimenuitem> </menuchoice>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:1143
#, no-c-format
msgid "Section:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:1144
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The section name is used to organize the file types in menus. This is also "
"used in the <menuchoice><guimenu>Tools</guimenu><guimenuitem>Filetypes</"
"guimenuitem> </menuchoice> menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:1150
#, no-c-format
msgid "Variables:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:1151
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This string allows you to configure &kappname;'s settings for the files "
"selected by this mimetype using &kappname; variables. You can set almost any "
"configuration option, such as highlight, indent-mode, etc."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:1155
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Press <guibutton>Edit</guibutton> to see a list of all available variables "
"and their descriptions. Select the checkbox on the left to enable a "
"particular variable and then set the value of the variable on the right. "
"Some variables provide a drop-down box to select possible values from while "
"others require you to enter a valid value manually."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:1160
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For complete information on these variables, see <link linkend=\"config-"
"variables\">Configuring with Document Variables</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:1167
#, no-c-format
msgid "Highlighting:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:1168
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you create a new file type, this drop down box allows you to select a "
"filetype for highlighting."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:1173
#, no-c-format
msgid "Indentation Mode:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:1174
#, no-c-format
msgid "The drop down box specifies the indentation mode for new documents."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:1179
#, no-c-format
msgid "File extensions:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:1180
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The wildcards mask allows you to select files by filename. A typical mask "
"uses an asterisk and the file extension, for example <filename>*.txt; *."
"text</filename>. The string is a semicolon-separated list of masks."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:1187
#, no-c-format
msgid "MIME types:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:1188
#, no-c-format
msgid "Displays a wizard that helps you easily select mimetypes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: configuring.docbook:1193
#, no-c-format
msgid "Priority:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:1194
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Sets a priority for this file type. If more than one file type selects the "
"same file, the one with the highest priority will be used."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: configuring.docbook:1203
#, no-c-format
msgid "Download Highlighting Files..."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:1205
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click this button to download new or updated syntax highlight descriptions "
"from the &kappname; website."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:1220
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuring With Document Variables"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:1222
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kappname; variables is katepart's implementation of document variables, "
"similar to &Emacs; and vi modelines. In katepart, the lines have the "
"following format: <userinput>kate: VARIABLENAME VALUE; [ VARIABLENAME "
"VALUE; ... ]</userinput> The lines can of course be in a comment, if the "
"file is in a format with comments. Variable names are single words (no "
"whitespace), and anything up to the next semicolon is the value. The "
"semicolon is required."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:1231
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here is an example variable line, forcing indentation settings for a C++, "
"java or javascript file:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: configuring.docbook:1234
#, no-c-format
msgid "// kate: replace-tabs on; indent-width 4; indent-mode cstyle;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:1237
#, no-c-format
msgid "Only the first and last 10 lines are searched for variable lines."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:1239
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Additionally, document variables can be placed in a file called <filename>."
"kateconfig</filename> in any directory, and the configured settings will be "
"applied as if the modelines were entered on every file in the directory and "
"its subdirectories, as far down as the <link linkend=\"pref-open-save-"
"advanced\">configured search depth.</link> Document variables in <filename>."
"kateconfig</filename> use the same syntax as in modelines."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:1247
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are variables to support almost all configurations in katepart, and "
"additionally plugins can use variables, in which case it should be "
"documented in the plugin's documentation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:1252
#, no-c-format
msgid "How &kappname; uses Variables"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:1254
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When reading configuration, katepart looks in the following places (in that "
"order): <itemizedlist> <listitem><para>The global configuration.</para></"
"listitem> <listitem><para>Optional session data.</para></listitem> "
"<listitem><para>The \"Filetype\" configuration.</para></listitem> "
"<listitem><para>Document variables in <filename>.kateconfig</filename>.</"
"para></listitem> <listitem><para>Document variables in the document itself.</"
"para></listitem> <listitem><para>Settings made during editing from menu or "
"command line.</para></listitem> </itemizedlist> As you can see, document "
"variables are only overridden by changes made at runtime. Whenever a "
"document is saved, the document variables are reread, and will overwrite "
"changes made using menu items or the command line."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:1270
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Any variable not listed below is stored in the document and can be queried "
"by other objects such as plugins, which can use them for their own purpose. "
"For example, the variable indent mode uses document variables for its "
"configuration."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:1275
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The variables listed here documents &kappname; version 3.7. More variables "
"may be added in the future. There are 3 possible types of values for "
"variables, with the following valid expressions:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:1279
#, no-c-format
msgid "BOOL - on|off|true|false|1|0"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:1280
#, no-c-format
msgid "INTEGER - any integer number"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:1281
#, no-c-format
msgid "STRING - anything else"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:1288
#, no-c-format
msgid "Available Variables"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#: configuring.docbook:1293
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>auto-center-lines</command><arg>INT</arg>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:1294
#, no-c-format
msgid "Set the number of autocenter lines."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#: configuring.docbook:1298
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>auto-insert-doxygen</command><arg>BOOL</arg>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:1299
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Turn insertion of the leading asterisk in doxygen comments on or off. This "
"has no effect unless you use the C-style auto-indenter."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: cmdsynopsis
#: configuring.docbook:1304
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>background-color</command><arg>STRING</arg>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:1305
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Set the document background color. The value must be something that can be "
"evaluated to a valid color, for example <userinput>#ff0000</userinput>."
